{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban car insurance premiums rises after theft through no fault of your own",
        "additional_details": "",
        "background": "In Canada car insurance premiums only increase if the claimant is at fault but in the UK your personal car insurance premiums can rise even when your car is stolen through no fault of your own and even if you do not make a claim. We believe this is wrong and requires regulation.",
